Destructuring
1. Destructuring Arrays
Extract values from arrays into variables easily:

js
Copy
Edit
const arr = [10, 20, 30];

// Basic destructuring
const [a, b, c] = arr;
console.log(a, b, c); // 10 20 30

// Skip elements
const [first, , third] = arr;
console.log(first, third); // 10 30

// Default values
const [x, y, z = 100] = [1, 2];
console.log(x, y, z); // 1 2 100
2. Destructuring Objects
Extract properties into variables by key names:

js
Copy
Edit
const user = {
  name: "Alice",
  age: 25,
  city: "NY"
};

// Basic destructuring
const { name, age } = user;
console.log(name, age); // Alice 25

// Rename variables
const { city: location } = user;
console.log(location); // NY

// Default values
const { country = "USA" } = user;
console.log(country); // USA
🔹 Spread ... Operator
Used to expand elements of arrays or objects.

1. Spread in Arrays
js
Copy
Edit
const arr1 = [1, 2];
const arr2 = [3, 4];

// Merge arrays
const merged = [...arr1, ...arr2];
console.log(merged); // [1, 2, 3, 4]

// Copy array (shallow copy)
const copy = [...arr1];
console.log(copy); // [1, 2]
2. Spread in Objects
js
Copy
Edit
const obj1 = { a: 1, b: 2 };
const obj2 = { c: 3, d: 4 };

// Merge objects
const mergedObj = { ...obj1, ...obj2 };
console.log(mergedObj); // { a:1, b:2, c:3, d:4 }

// Copy object (shallow copy)
const copyObj = { ...obj1 };
console.log(copyObj); // { a:1, b:2 }
Note: If keys overlap, later values overwrite earlier ones.

js
Copy
Edit
const o1 = { a: 1, b: 2 };
const o2 = { b: 10, c: 3 };

const merged = { ...o1, ...o2 };
console.log(merged); // { a: 1, b: 10, c: 3 }
🔹 Rest ... Operator
Used to collect remaining elements into an array or object.

1. Rest with Arrays
js
Copy
Edit
const [first, ...rest] = [10, 20, 30, 40];
console.log(first); // 10
console.log(rest);  // [20, 30, 40]
2. Rest with Objects
js
Copy
Edit
const { a, b, ...rest } = { a: 1, b: 2, c: 3, d: 4 };
console.log(a, b);   // 1 2
console.log(rest);   // { c: 3, d: 4 }